1
00:00:01,820 --> 00:00:06,760
Alchemy, the science of understanding,
deconstructing, and reconstructing matter.

2
00:00:06,880 --> 00:00:09,880
However, it is not an all-powerful art.

3
00:00:10,060 --> 00:00:12,820
It is impossible to create
something out of nothing.

4
00:00:12,940 --> 00:00:17,320
If one wishes to obtain something,
something of equal value must be given.

5
00:00:17,380 --> 00:00:21,500
This is the law of equivalent exchange,
the basis of all alchemy.

6
00:00:21,640 --> 00:00:24,980
In accordance with this law,
there is a taboo among alchemists.

7
00:00:25,040 --> 00:00:27,580
Human transmutation is strictly forbidden.

8
00:00:27,620 --> 00:00:30,860
For what could equal the value
of a human soul?

9
00:00:31,580 --> 00:00:35,060
Kono omoi wo keshite shimau niwa

10
00:00:35,060 --> 00:00:37,400
mada jinsei nagai dsho?

11
00:00:38,380 --> 00:00:43,840
Yarinokoshite'ru koto
yarinaoshite mitai kara

12
00:00:53,600 --> 00:00:59,840
Yume no tsuzuki oikakete ita hazu na no ni

13
00:01:00,160 --> 00:01:06,180
Magarikunetta
hosoi michi hito ni tsumazuku

14
00:01:06,180 --> 00:01:13,100
Ano koro mitai ni tte modoritai wake ja nai ni
Nakushite kita sora wo sagashite'ru

15
00:01:13,100 --> 00:01:14,720
Wakatte kuremasu you ni

16
00:01:14,720 --> 00:01:19,880
Gisei ni natta you na
kanashii kao wa yamete yo

17
00:01:19,880 --> 00:01:23,340
Tsumi no saigo wa namida ja nai yo
Zutto kurushiku seotte'ku n da

18
00:01:23,340 --> 00:01:26,720
Deguchi mienai kanjou meiro ni
dare wo matte'ru no?

19
00:01:26,720 --> 00:01:30,300
Shiroi nooto ni tsuzutta you ni
motto sunao ni hakidashitai yo

20
00:01:30,300 --> 00:01:33,440
Nani kar nogaretai n da
genjitsu tte yatsu?

21
00:01:33,440 --> 00:01:40,140
Kanaeru tame ni ikite'ru n datte
Sakebitaku naru yo Kikoete imasu ka?

22
00:01:40,160 --> 00:01:45,240
Bunai n nante yatte'rarenai kara

23
00:01:45,280 --> 00:01:47,120
...kaeru basho mo nai no

24
00:01:47,120 --> 00:01:50,420
Yasashisa niwa itsumo kansha shite'ru

25
00:01:50,420 --> 00:01:53,900
Dakara tsuyoku naritai
(I'm on the way)

26
00:01:53,900 --> 00:01:57,560
Natsukashiku naru
konna itami mo kangei jan

27
00:02:01,760 --> 00:02:06,320
The town of Liore had fallen under
the control of Father Cornello,

28
00:02:06,340 --> 00:02:11,680
A corrupt priest who used alchemy combined
with a Philosopher's Stone to deceive his people.

29
00:02:11,820 --> 00:02:16,020
Ed and Al came to Liore and put
a stop to the priest's sinister plans.

30
00:02:16,080 --> 00:02:19,320
The Philosopher's Stone, however,
was revealed to be a fake.

31
00:02:19,560 --> 00:02:23,780
Their leader exposed as a fraud,
the hopes of the citizens of Liore were crushed.

32
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:26,400
"Stand up and walk. Move forward."

33
00:02:26,560 --> 00:02:31,180
These were Ed's words to Rose, words
he had once needed to hear himself.

34
00:02:43,060 --> 00:02:46,580
You are Basque Grand,
the Iron Blood Alchemist, correct?

35
00:02:46,820 --> 00:02:48,620
Why? Who's asking?

36
00:02:49,780 --> 00:02:53,380
Foolish alchemists who have
turned their backs on the ways of God...

37
00:02:53,380 --> 00:02:54,860
Shall all be punished.

38
00:02:54,860 --> 00:03:01,040
I see. You must be the bloodthirsty murderer who's been
making a habit of targeting State Alchemists, lately.

39
00:03:03,160 --> 00:03:06,640
Well, this time,
you picked the wrong target!

40
00:03:17,600 --> 00:03:19,400
You're fast...
Try this!

41
00:03:22,500 --> 00:03:23,900
A little more?!

42
00:03:28,000 --> 00:03:30,800
Hmph.
That wasn't so difficult.

43
00:03:40,160 --> 00:03:42,780
What?
No! How?!

44
00:03:42,800 --> 00:03:44,300
Now you perish.

45
00:03:56,520 --> 00:03:58,560
HUGHES: Another State Alchemist dead.

46
00:03:59,160 --> 00:04:01,400
ARMSTRONG: This killer is highly skilled.

47
00:04:01,400 --> 00:04:03,340
For all we know, you could
be the next one he comes after.
HUGHES: Major, you watch yourself.

48
00:04:06,960 --> 00:04:08,140
Understood.

49
00:04:08,140 --> 00:04:09,680
[CAR APPROACHING]

50
00:04:13,700 --> 00:04:17,300
Fuhrer Bradley, Your Excellency.
What brings you here?

51
00:04:19,500 --> 00:04:21,300
BRADLEY: I got word of what happened.

52
00:04:22,240 --> 00:04:25,520
Lt. Colonel Hughes, you're
the officer in charge of this case?

53
00:04:25,520 --> 00:04:26,300
Yes, sir.

54
00:04:26,780 --> 00:04:29,660
Should you need any
additional personnel, just ask.

55
00:04:30,380 --> 00:04:33,900
The man doing this is a traitor.
I want him stopped.

56
00:04:34,920 --> 00:04:35,880
Sir.

57
00:04:36,000 --> 00:04:37,880
[BIRDS CHIRPING]

58
00:04:39,360 --> 00:04:40,280
Lieutenant Breda.

59
00:04:40,300 --> 00:04:40,920
Right.

60
00:04:42,340 --> 00:04:46,140
Jeez. The Colonel's sure letting
his work pile up again, huh?

61
00:04:46,880 --> 00:04:49,200
Havoc, give me a hand, will ya?

62
00:04:49,300 --> 00:04:51,680
I've got plenty to do over here already.

63
00:04:52,140 --> 00:04:54,300
Next up...
Who's this?

64
00:04:54,300 --> 00:04:55,300
FALMAN:
Lieutenant Yoki.

65
00:04:55,880 --> 00:05:00,540
Remember? The crook who was using the Youswell
coal mine concessions to line his own pockets?

66
00:05:00,820 --> 00:05:05,100
Anyway, the Elric brothers exposed what that
dirty thief was up to and now he's on the run.

67
00:05:05,160 --> 00:05:06,080
[RADIO STATIC]

68
00:05:06,080 --> 00:05:08,100
Master Sergeant Fuery,
how's the radio?

69
00:05:08,460 --> 00:05:12,300
The receiver on this thing's seen better days.
I think I'm gonna have to replace it.

70
00:05:15,420 --> 00:05:16,180
Huh?

71
00:05:16,720 --> 00:05:18,500
Hey, it's Edward and Alphonse!

72
00:05:18,580 --> 00:05:20,300
HAWKEYE: Welcome back, boys.

73
00:05:20,420 --> 00:05:22,200
Go on in.
The Colonel's expecting you.

74
00:05:24,180 --> 00:05:26,880
Well done on the Lior case,
you two. Nice work.

75
00:05:26,880 --> 00:05:28,700
I appreciate you
resolving the matter.

76
00:05:28,960 --> 00:05:31,300
No big deal.
It's not like we did it for you.

77
00:05:31,460 --> 00:05:34,980
Right. The Philosopher's Stone.
Another false lead?

78
00:05:38,760 --> 00:05:41,020
Yeah, after all that,
the Stone was a fake.

79
00:05:41,060 --> 00:05:44,380
Even so, the power it gave Cornello
was real enough.

80
00:05:44,460 --> 00:05:47,140
He transmuted this huge
Chimera right in front of us.

81
00:05:47,360 --> 00:05:50,240
I still wonder how he was
able to use the Stone to do that.

82
00:05:50,540 --> 00:05:54,400
I'm not familiar enough with the field of
bioalchemy to really understand it.

83
00:05:54,560 --> 00:05:58,300
Yeah, I'm kinda curious about that, too.
It might be worth looking into.

84
00:05:58,480 --> 00:06:01,780
Who knows? Maybe we'll find something
that could help us restore our bodies.

85
00:06:01,780 --> 00:06:02,300
AL: Mmm!

86
00:06:02,450 --> 00:06:05,080
It might help if you
consulted a specialist.

87
00:06:05,140 --> 00:06:05,860
BOTH: Huh?

88
00:06:06,760 --> 00:06:09,310
The Sewing Life Alchemist, Shou Tucker.

89
00:06:09,400 --> 00:06:13,340
He's done some heavy research into
Chimera transmutation. I'll introduce you.

90
00:06:13,800 --> 00:06:15,220
You would do that for us?!

91
00:06:15,220 --> 00:06:18,040
Okay, what's the catch?
You want something, don't you?

92
00:06:18,040 --> 00:06:22,020
Don't doubt my motives. I'm trying to
repay you for your work on the Lior case!

93
00:06:22,440 --> 00:06:25,160
Doing you a favor is better
than being indebted to you.

94
00:06:26,860 --> 00:06:31,300
MUSTANG: Two years ago, Tucker transmuted a
Chimera that could understand human speech.

95
00:06:31,480 --> 00:06:34,120
That earned him his
certification as a State Alchemist.

96
00:06:34,140 --> 00:06:36,500
By understand human speech.
You mean...

97
00:06:36,500 --> 00:06:39,140
Wait, you mean it talks?!
A Chimera?

98
00:06:39,260 --> 00:06:40,140
Right.

99
00:06:40,380 --> 00:06:41,980
Supposedly...

100
00:06:41,980 --> 00:06:43,700
It only said one thing.

101
00:06:44,580 --> 00:06:46,020
"I want to die."

102
00:06:48,080 --> 00:06:52,100
After that, it refused to eat
until it got its wish.

103
00:06:52,160 --> 00:06:54,100
[DOORBELL RINGING]

104
00:06:55,400 --> 00:06:57,560
ED: Man, this house is huge.

105
00:06:58,440 --> 00:06:58,880
Huh?

106
00:06:58,880 --> 00:07:00,280
[HOWLING]

107
00:07:00,280 --> 00:07:02,000
[ED YELPING]

108
00:07:02,280 --> 00:07:03,920
You okay, Ed?!

109
00:07:03,920 --> 00:07:04,720
Daddy!

110
00:07:04,720 --> 00:07:05,480
Huh?

111
00:07:05,720 --> 00:07:08,040
There are people out here. Look!

112
00:07:08,060 --> 00:07:11,600
Nina, this is why I told
you to keep the dog tied up.

113
00:07:14,760 --> 00:07:16,400
I'm sorry about the mess.

114
00:07:16,420 --> 00:07:19,260
Ever since my wife ran out,
this place has been a wreck.

115
00:07:19,500 --> 00:07:21,300
I'm not much of a housekeeper.

116
00:07:26,120 --> 00:07:26,920
[SIGHS]

117
00:07:26,920 --> 00:07:30,380
Now that we're all settled in, let me
say that it's a pleasure to meet you, Edward.

118
00:07:30,600 --> 00:07:33,820
As the Colonel told you, I'm the
Sewing Life Alchemist, Shou Tucker.

119
00:07:34,440 --> 00:07:36,860
Ed is interested in the
field of biologic alchemy.

120
00:07:37,080 --> 00:07:39,740
He would like to have a look at
your research, if that's possible.

121
00:07:39,960 --> 00:07:42,020
Oh, yes, certainly.
I don't mind.

122
00:07:43,520 --> 00:07:44,420
However...

123
00:07:45,500 --> 00:07:48,160
If you want me to show you
the tricks I've got up my sleeve,

124
00:07:48,160 --> 00:07:51,300
it's only fair you show me the
tricks you've got up yours as well.

125
00:07:51,520 --> 00:07:54,480
It's the code we live by,
equivalent exchange.

126
00:07:54,760 --> 00:07:57,540
Now, why are you interested
in bioalchemy?

127
00:07:57,720 --> 00:08:00,340
Oh, um, Ed...
Well, you see, he's...

128
00:08:00,340 --> 00:08:01,320
Colonel.

129
00:08:04,660 --> 00:08:06,700
You transmuted your mother?

130
00:08:06,940 --> 00:08:09,300
As an eleven-year-old child?

131
00:08:10,300 --> 00:08:11,300
I see.

132
00:08:11,620 --> 00:08:14,420
So that's what earned you the title
"Fullmetal Alchemist."

133
00:08:15,600 --> 00:08:17,960
You've had a rough time of it
for someone so young.

134
00:08:22,300 --> 00:08:23,140
[SIGHS]

135
00:08:23,140 --> 00:08:26,080
I can't say for sure if it's going
to be of any use to you or not...

136
00:08:27,020 --> 00:08:30,300
But why don't you go ahead
and take a look at my laboratory?

137
00:08:30,300 --> 00:08:34,000
[VARIOUS ANIMALS SNARLING, GROWLING,
SCREECHING AND SQUAWKING]

138
00:08:34,000 --> 00:08:35,420
AL: Oh...!

139
00:08:35,600 --> 00:08:37,300
TUCKER: It's kind of embarrassing.

140
00:08:37,580 --> 00:08:40,840
I'm fairly widely regarded
as an authority on Chimeras...

141
00:08:40,840 --> 00:08:45,300
But the truth is, it hasn't actually
been going that well lately.

142
00:08:48,060 --> 00:08:50,000
ED: Oh... amazing!

143
00:08:50,040 --> 00:08:52,600
TUCKER: This is my library.
Feel free to look around.

144
00:08:52,600 --> 00:08:55,300
All right, let's dive in!
I'll start with this shelf.

145
00:08:55,400 --> 00:08:57,180
I'll try starting over here!

146
00:08:58,740 --> 00:09:00,560
I'm going to head back to work now.

147
00:09:00,640 --> 00:09:03,140
I'll send somebody by
to get you this evening.

148
00:09:06,540 --> 00:09:08,420
They've got some ability to focus.

149
00:09:08,580 --> 00:09:11,140
I'm not sure they even
know we're here anymore.

150
00:09:12,920 --> 00:09:16,180
Quite a catch, these two.
A couple of prodigies.

151
00:09:18,160 --> 00:09:21,260
[CLOCK TICKING]

152
00:09:28,540 --> 00:09:29,580
Hmm?
[NINA GASPS]

153
00:09:34,860 --> 00:09:35,740
[GIGGLE]

154
00:09:36,880 --> 00:09:39,580
[NINA GIGGLING]

155
00:09:42,020 --> 00:09:44,120
Woo- hoo! Way up high!
[AL AND NINA GIGGLING]

156
00:09:45,480 --> 00:09:48,200
Al! What are you doing?
You're supposed to be reading!

157
00:09:48,700 --> 00:09:51,300
Uh...Nina looked like she
wanted to play!

158
00:09:51,300 --> 00:09:54,060
Well, in case you forgot, we
didn't come here to play horsey!

159
00:09:54,580 --> 00:09:55,840
Huh?
[DOG HOWLS]

160
00:09:55,840 --> 00:09:57,250
[ED YELPING]

161
00:09:59,580 --> 00:10:02,300
Alexander says that he
wants to play too!

162
00:10:03,940 --> 00:10:05,380
That's what you want, is it?

163
00:10:06,280 --> 00:10:08,220
You've bested me twice, dog...

164
00:10:08,300 --> 00:10:09,680
But playtime is over.

165
00:10:09,720 --> 00:10:11,540
I will not lose this time!

166
00:10:11,540 --> 00:10:15,300
I, Edward Elric, will use my considerable
powers to vanquish you!

167
00:10:15,360 --> 00:10:17,620
You mangy mutt!

168
00:10:17,740 --> 00:10:20,240
[GIGGLING]

169
00:10:20,940 --> 00:10:23,300
Hey, Chief!
Your ride has arrived.

170
00:10:25,760 --> 00:10:27,440
What are you up to
down there, Ed?

171
00:10:27,520 --> 00:10:31,740
Oh, uh...let's just say I'm taking a
break from a long day of research.

172
00:10:32,620 --> 00:10:35,300
After all that,
you must be dog tired.

173
00:10:35,740 --> 00:10:37,000
[LAUGHING]

174
00:10:37,000 --> 00:10:39,020
Why don't you come
on back tomorrow?

175
00:10:39,020 --> 00:10:40,760
[GASPS]
You're really going to come again?!

176
00:10:40,760 --> 00:10:42,740
We'll play some more tomorrow!
Okay, Nina?

177
00:10:42,740 --> 00:10:43,560
'Kay!

178
00:10:45,400 --> 00:10:48,680
Oh, Mr. Tucker, I almost forgot.
I've got a message for you.

179
00:10:48,700 --> 00:10:52,900
It's from the Colonel. He says,"Don't forget,
Assessment day is coming soon."

180
00:10:53,480 --> 00:10:55,880
Yes. Please assure him I know.

181
00:10:56,120 --> 00:10:56,920
Right.

182
00:11:03,380 --> 00:11:04,540
Hey, Daddy?

183
00:11:05,860 --> 00:11:07,900
What does
"Assessment Day" mean?

184
00:11:11,200 --> 00:11:15,780
State Alchemists have to report on their research
once a year in order to keep their certification.

185
00:11:17,820 --> 00:11:21,400
You see, last year, Nina, your
daddy didn't get a very good evaluation.

186
00:11:21,760 --> 00:11:26,320
Unless I do something really impressive this year,
I won't be a State Alchemist anymore.

187
00:11:26,420 --> 00:11:29,680
Huh? No, you'll
do just fine, Daddy!

188
00:11:29,680 --> 00:11:32,580
I know you will,
you're always studying so much!

189
00:11:32,800 --> 00:11:37,980
[CHUCKLES]
You're right, Nina. I have to try hard.

190
00:11:39,200 --> 00:11:41,260
Or we'll be left with nothing...

191
00:11:41,260 --> 00:11:42,180
Again.

192
00:11:43,320 --> 00:11:44,920
Fullmetal Alchemist.

193
00:11:46,420 --> 00:11:48,140
Fullmetal Alchemist.

194
00:11:48,500 --> 00:11:50,520
[BIRDS CHIRPING]

195
00:11:50,940 --> 00:11:53,500
AL: Your mother
left two years ago?

196
00:11:54,240 --> 00:11:57,160
Daddy said she went back
to live at her parents' house.

197
00:11:57,600 --> 00:12:02,000
It must get kind of lonely with just you
and your dad living in this big house, huh?

198
00:12:02,300 --> 00:12:04,200
Mm-mm. Not really.

199
00:12:04,200 --> 00:12:08,300
Daddy's so nice, and plus
I've got Alexander to play with, too!

200
00:12:09,820 --> 00:12:13,300
But lately, Daddy's been
studying in his lab all the time...

201
00:12:13,580 --> 00:12:16,460
I guess that does
make me a little bit lonely.

202
00:12:23,040 --> 00:12:26,300
[YAWNING]
My shoulders are killing me.

203
00:12:26,640 --> 00:12:29,120
Maybe you should try to
move around some, brother.

204
00:12:29,140 --> 00:12:31,100
Yeah, not a bad idea, Al.

205
00:12:31,180 --> 00:12:32,660
Hey, you mangy mutt!

206
00:12:32,660 --> 00:12:33,300
[BARKS]

207
00:12:33,720 --> 00:12:35,840
Looks like you could
use some exercise.

208
00:12:35,880 --> 00:12:37,460
[AL GIGGLES]
Let's go, too, Nina!

209
00:12:39,780 --> 00:12:40,820
[GIGGLE]

210
00:12:40,940 --> 00:12:42,840
[ED YELLING PLAYFULLY]
C'mon, c'mon!

211
00:12:42,840 --> 00:12:44,520
ED: C'mon, you can't catch me!
NINA: Wait up!

212
00:12:44,520 --> 00:12:45,620
C'mon, slowpokes!

213
00:12:47,960 --> 00:12:49,200
Ha-ha!

214
00:12:49,300 --> 00:12:52,120
I'm gonna get you!
Look out! Here I come!

215
00:12:52,300 --> 00:12:54,300
[AL AND NINA GIGGLING]

216
00:12:54,300 --> 00:12:55,820
ED: [MUFFLED GRUNT]
AL: Huh?

217
00:12:55,940 --> 00:12:58,180
[GIGGLING]

218
00:13:00,360 --> 00:13:04,560
[SOUNDS OF PLAYING
CONTINUE IN THE DISTANCE]

219
00:13:07,680 --> 00:13:10,360
"Don't forget, Assessment Day
is coming soon."

220
00:13:18,880 --> 00:13:22,920
HUGHES: What I wanna know is why this guy is only
targeting State Alchemists and no one else.

221
00:13:23,520 --> 00:13:27,720
If it's the military he's trying to hurt,
he could go after normal soldiers.

222
00:13:28,040 --> 00:13:31,440
Surely soldiers would be easier
to kill than highly skilled Alchemists...

223
00:13:31,480 --> 00:13:34,300
especially ones that
have been State-certified.

224
00:13:35,120 --> 00:13:37,700
Maybe the certification
is the reason.

225
00:13:37,840 --> 00:13:38,320
Hmm?

226
00:13:38,400 --> 00:13:41,300
State Alchemists are given
high pay and special privilege.

227
00:13:41,440 --> 00:13:44,620
There must be any number of people
who envy them for their positions.

228
00:13:44,840 --> 00:13:49,600
Or perhaps they feel they have not upheld
their creed, "Alchemist be thou for the people."

229
00:13:49,760 --> 00:13:56,740
Alchemists who are supposed to be pillars of science and truth are
turned into the military's walking weapons as soon as they receive certification.

230
00:13:57,800 --> 00:13:59,580
There are plenty of people, I'm sure...

231
00:13:59,600 --> 00:14:03,920
Who have not forgotten the role that
State Alchemists played in the Ishvalan Civil War

232
00:14:04,100 --> 00:14:05,120
[KNOCKING ON DOOR]

233
00:14:06,660 --> 00:14:08,100
I have a report, sir.

234
00:14:08,400 --> 00:14:12,580
A canvas has revealed that yesterday,
at 9.30, or right around that time,

235
00:14:12,580 --> 00:14:18,080
a man with a large scar on his face was sighted in the
Central City train station by multiple station employees.

236
00:14:18,100 --> 00:14:21,160
The station?!
Looks like that bastard got away.

237
00:14:23,780 --> 00:14:27,660
Before I earned my State Alchemist
certification, our life was terrible.

238
00:14:28,500 --> 00:14:30,460
We were so poor in those days.

239
00:14:31,550 --> 00:14:36,120
My wife couldn't stand living that
kind of life, so she left us.

240
00:14:38,880 --> 00:14:41,180
I can't afford to
fail this assessment.

241
00:14:41,760 --> 00:14:44,960
I don't wanna go back to those days again.
I don't even think I could.

242
00:14:45,300 --> 00:14:47,300
Don't worry, Daddy,
it's okay!

243
00:14:47,300 --> 00:14:52,180
If those people do tell you no, me and
Alexander will growl at them until they say yes!

244
00:14:52,320 --> 00:14:54,920
[AL GIGGLING]
You tell 'em, Nina!

245
00:14:55,900 --> 00:14:59,700
Hey, Nina. I've got an idea.
Do you want to play with Daddy tomorrow?

246
00:14:59,820 --> 00:15:01,060
Really?!

247
00:15:01,180 --> 00:15:02,060
Yeah.

248
00:15:02,360 --> 00:15:04,060
Woo-hoo!

249
00:15:04,320 --> 00:15:08,180
Alexander! Daddy says he's
going to play with us tomorrow!

250
00:15:08,260 --> 00:15:10,520
[ALEXANDER BARKS]
[ED AND AL CHUCKLING]

251
00:15:12,000 --> 00:15:14,300
[DOORBELL RINGING]

252
00:15:19,460 --> 00:15:23,300
Hello, Mr. Tucker!
Thanks for having us again today!

253
00:15:23,940 --> 00:15:24,860
Huh?

254
00:15:26,860 --> 00:15:28,300
Mr. Tucker?

255
00:15:28,320 --> 00:15:30,300
Hey! Nina?!

256
00:15:31,300 --> 00:15:32,140
[DOOR OPENS]

257
00:15:33,120 --> 00:15:34,300
AL: Mr. Tucker!

258
00:15:34,320 --> 00:15:36,300
ED: There you are!
So you are home.

259
00:15:37,300 --> 00:15:38,300
Yes.

260
00:15:38,900 --> 00:15:41,980
I did it, boys.
I finally did it.

261
00:15:42,900 --> 00:15:45,600
A Chimera that
understands human speech.

262
00:15:48,390 --> 00:15:49,480
Here, let me show you.

263
00:15:49,980 --> 00:15:53,700
Listen to me.
That person over there, that's Edward.

264
00:15:53,720 --> 00:15:56,700
That person... Edward...

265
00:15:56,720 --> 00:15:59,100
Yes, that's very good. Well done!

266
00:15:59,160 --> 00:16:01,780
That's amazing!
It can actually talk!

267
00:16:01,800 --> 00:16:06,060
Now I don't have to worry
about losing my certification!

268
00:16:06,660 --> 00:16:09,500
That person Ed...ward...

269
00:16:09,900 --> 00:16:11,120
Woah...

270
00:16:12,220 --> 00:16:17,760
That person Ed...ward...
That person Ed...ward...

271
00:16:18,460 --> 00:16:20,420
Big brother, Ed...

272
00:16:20,420 --> 00:16:21,920
[GASP]

273
00:16:29,900 --> 00:16:33,920
ED: Mr. Tucker, when did you
first get your state certification?

274
00:16:34,020 --> 00:16:37,200
Let's see...
It was two years ago.

275
00:16:38,900 --> 00:16:41,280
And when did your wife leave you?

276
00:16:42,160 --> 00:16:43,940
That was two years ago, too.

277
00:16:44,520 --> 00:16:47,300
I just have one more
question for you.

278
00:16:47,350 --> 00:16:50,700
Nina and Alexander... Where are they?!

279
00:16:50,720 --> 00:16:51,500
[GASP]

280
00:16:55,160 --> 00:16:57,300
Damn brat, figuring it out so quickly.

281
00:16:59,160 --> 00:17:00,060
Brother!

282
00:17:00,260 --> 00:17:03,520
Oh yeah, I figured it out!
You did it again!

283
00:17:03,940 --> 00:17:06,300
Two years ago, it was your wife,

284
00:17:06,300 --> 00:17:11,040
This time, you used your own daughter
and her dog to transmute a talking Chimera!

285
00:17:11,180 --> 00:17:14,100
You can only do so much
with animals, after all.

286
00:17:14,300 --> 00:17:17,680
It's much easier when you start
with a human, isn't that right?

287
00:17:18,440 --> 00:17:22,380
I don't see what you're so upset about.
This is how we progress.

288
00:17:22,420 --> 00:17:25,660
Human experimentation
is a necessary step.

289
00:17:25,700 --> 00:17:28,420
I would think a scientist
should understand—

290
00:17:28,460 --> 00:17:31,800
ED: Shut up! Do you really think
you can get away with this?!

291
00:17:31,980 --> 00:17:35,990
Messing around with someone's
life like that... Your own daughter!

292
00:17:36,080 --> 00:17:37,660
Someone's life, you say?

293
00:17:37,820 --> 00:17:40,660
[LAUGHS] You'd know all about that,
wouldn't you?

294
00:17:40,820 --> 00:17:43,900
Look at you, Fullmetal Alchemist,
look at your legs...

295
00:17:43,960 --> 00:17:44,940
Your arm...

296
00:17:44,940 --> 00:17:46,120
Your brother...

297
00:17:46,280 --> 00:17:51,000
Those things are also the result of messing
around with somebody's life, aren't they?

298
00:17:51,000 --> 00:17:52,100
Shut up!

299
00:17:54,920 --> 00:17:59,230
[CACKLES] We are the same!
We're the same! You're just like me!

300
00:17:59,440 --> 00:18:00,260
We're not!

301
00:18:00,260 --> 00:18:04,540
Oh, but yes we are! The opportunity
was right in front of us and we took it!

302
00:18:04,640 --> 00:18:07,560
We had to, even though we
knew it was against the rules!

303
00:18:07,640 --> 00:18:08,500
No!

304
00:18:09,700 --> 00:18:10,860
Not me!

305
00:18:11,200 --> 00:18:12,700
Alchemists don't...

306
00:18:13,580 --> 00:18:15,180
Do that!

307
00:18:15,720 --> 00:18:18,720
I'm not... I'm not!

308
00:18:18,720 --> 00:18:20,360
Brother!

309
00:18:20,360 --> 00:18:22,800
If you keep this up,
he'll die!

310
00:18:33,700 --> 00:18:35,580
Edward, no...

311
00:18:36,920 --> 00:18:41,600
Daddy...
Do you... hurt... Daddy?

312
00:18:48,000 --> 00:18:54,380
I'm sorry. Even with all our power,
we can't do anything to change you back.

313
00:18:54,780 --> 00:18:56,240
I'm sorry....

314
00:18:56,820 --> 00:18:58,120
I'm sorry.

315
00:18:58,480 --> 00:19:02,140
Can we play...now?
Can we play now?

316
00:19:03,160 --> 00:19:04,880
I made it just in time.

317
00:19:05,020 --> 00:19:08,140
I get to remain a
State Alchemist...I passed!

318
00:19:16,340 --> 00:19:19,080
[PATHETIC WHIMPERING]

319
00:19:20,080 --> 00:19:24,300
Like hell you're staying a State Alchemist...
Like hell.

320
00:19:25,920 --> 00:19:27,940
Can we... play now?

321
00:19:30,740 --> 00:19:33,960
[PAINED YELLING]
Damn it!

322
00:19:37,340 --> 00:19:40,580
HAWKEYE: If there was an example
of the devil's work in this world...

323
00:19:40,760 --> 00:19:43,020
this world, this case would
definitely be it.

324
00:19:43,540 --> 00:19:45,120
MUSTANG: The devil, huh?

325
00:19:45,550 --> 00:19:48,120
A State Alchemist must
be willing to act,

326
00:19:48,240 --> 00:19:51,920
Able to take another's life
when ordered to, without questioning.

327
00:19:52,280 --> 00:19:57,200
In some ways, Mr. Tucker's actions
and our own may not be all that far apart.

328
00:19:57,560 --> 00:20:00,480
When it comes to interfering
with other people's lives...

329
00:20:00,820 --> 00:20:03,980
We choose our own path,
knowing full well what we're doing.

330
00:20:06,380 --> 00:20:09,720
That's the way it is.
Right, Fullmetal?

331
00:20:14,280 --> 00:20:18,240
You will more than likely come
across cases like this again in the future.

332
00:20:18,520 --> 00:20:21,860
And you may end up having to
get your own hands dirty, as well.

333
00:20:22,720 --> 00:20:25,000
You gonna shut down
like this every time?

334
00:20:25,200 --> 00:20:27,630
We may be called dogs
of the military...

335
00:20:27,760 --> 00:20:29,860
We may even be
cursed as devils.

336
00:20:30,040 --> 00:20:31,200
It doesn't matter.

337
00:20:31,280 --> 00:20:34,180
Al and I are still going to
get our bodies back.

338
00:20:34,580 --> 00:20:36,600
We know the truth.

339
00:20:36,780 --> 00:20:40,880
We know we're not devils.
We know we're not gods.

340
00:20:41,920 --> 00:20:43,120
We're human.

341
00:20:45,280 --> 00:20:48,300
We're only human!

342
00:20:50,620 --> 00:20:54,070
We can't even do anything
to save one innocent little girl.

343
00:20:55,840 --> 00:20:57,840
So what good are we, then?

344
00:21:00,160 --> 00:21:03,160
I wonder why no one's
capable of understanding me.

345
00:21:04,280 --> 00:21:05,340
Nina...

346
00:21:09,220 --> 00:21:11,840
[THUNDER CRACKS]

347
00:21:11,860 --> 00:21:13,760
You're Shou Tucker, correct?

348
00:21:13,960 --> 00:21:18,620
Who are you? Not military.
Who are you?!

349
00:21:18,920 --> 00:21:22,380
How did you get in here?
There were military police out front!

350
00:21:23,360 --> 00:21:26,820
Foolish alchemists who turn
their backs on the ways of God...

351
00:21:28,940 --> 00:21:30,500
...shall be punished.

352
00:21:39,120 --> 00:21:40,900
Daddy's hurting...

353
00:21:42,940 --> 00:21:46,880
Daddy hurts...
No, daddy...

354
00:21:47,840 --> 00:21:49,360
You poor creature.

355
00:21:49,440 --> 00:21:53,380
Once you have been given this form,
there is no way of separating you again.

356
00:21:54,350 --> 00:21:59,940
At least your passing will be in peace.
[THUNDER CRACKS]

357
00:22:04,220 --> 00:22:05,000
God,

358
00:22:06,660 --> 00:22:07,680
Hear me.

359
00:22:08,060 --> 00:22:10,960
Two human souls have
just been returned to you.

360
00:22:11,540 --> 00:22:13,990
Please accept them
into your loving arms.

361
00:22:14,220 --> 00:22:18,620
Please grant these poor lost souls
everlasting peace and salvation.

362
00:22:19,800 --> 00:22:22,300
[THUNDER RUMBLING]

363
00:22:28,580 --> 00:22:34,400
Ano hi mita sora akaneiro no sora o

364
00:22:34,480 --> 00:22:39,700
nee kimi wa oboete imasu ka

365
00:22:39,760 --> 00:22:45,460
Yakusoku chigiri shoka
no kaze ga tsutsumu

366
00:22:45,720 --> 00:22:50,600
futari yorisotta

367
00:22:53,680 --> 00:22:58,860
Muri na egao no ura

368
00:22:58,860 --> 00:23:04,240
nobita kage o kakumau

369
00:23:04,280 --> 00:23:13,620
Dakara kizukanu furi saisei o erabu

370
00:23:15,700 --> 00:23:22,840
Table no ue no furuenai shirase machitsuzukete

371
00:23:26,260 --> 00:23:31,680
kuuhaku no yoru o kuru hazu no nai asa mo

372
00:23:31,680 --> 00:23:35,980
zenbu wakatte'tan da

373
00:23:36,060 --> 00:23:41,540
Ano hi mita sora akaneiro no sora o

374
00:23:41,540 --> 00:23:46,740
nee itsuka omoidasu deshou

375
00:23:46,740 --> 00:23:52,180
Hatasenakatta yakusoku o idaite

376
00:23:52,420 --> 00:23:57,240
futari arukidasu

377
00:23:59,200 --> 00:24:03,400
The rain pours down in East City.

378
00:24:03,400 --> 00:24:09,520
Still grief-stricken over the death of Nina,
Ed and Al are attacked by the mysterious man, Scar.

379
00:24:10,020 --> 00:24:15,740
In a moment of crisis, Ed must make a desperate decision
while the life of his brother hangs in the balance.

380
00:24:15,860 --> 00:24:18,920
Next time on
Fullmetal Alchemist: Brotherhood

381
00:24:19,020 --> 00:24:21,960
Episode 5, Rain of Sorrows

382
00:24:23,020 --> 00:24:25,100
What will Edward decide?

383
00:24:25,280 --> 00:24:28,400
And will he be able to
live with the consequences?
